⟦ validation_gates | VSL-LANG-GATES-v1.0 | vsm-1.2.1 | 2026-09-27T23:20:47Z ⟧

@vsm 1.2.1
@status ratified
// s5-policy/vsl-language/validation_gates.vsm — who enforces what, and over
// which corpus. Source: vsl_language §7b. Item of the reference set.
// C1/C5/C6 (what makes a file valid) stay in boot/vsl_language_primer.vsm.
// This file is for VALIDATOR operators, not for writers.

validation_gates("VSL-LANG-GATES") {

  gates: "
    encoding    @gate_encoding
      checks    UTF-8 ∧ NFC ∧ no BOM ∧ no invisible(NBSP,ZWSP,ZWNJ,ZWJ)
                ∧ ⟦ 4 pipe-separated fields ⟧ header ∧ footer
      blocking  YES ▪ corpus: every .vsm
      not covers   dash and prime discipline — ADVISORY only. A regex cannot
                tell a closing quote from a prime (S5′ vs '…S5').
      waives    covenant.vsm — constitutional signature, declared exception

    closure     @gate_closure
      checks    ∀ glyph g ∈ doc: g ∈ notation ▪ predicate arity consistent
      blocking  YES ▪ corpus: the primer
      not covers   term closure ADVISORY — shipped advisory because a
                37-false-positive gate is ignored within a week, and an
                ignored gate is worse than none. Also not: block structure ▪
                logical coherence. THOSE ARE READ, not checked.

    staleness   @gate_staleness
      checks    source-file hashes vs the last-verified manifest
      blocking  production track YES ▪ spec_revision track NO — advisory
                while under construction
      not covers   whether the primer's CONTENT is correct — verifies the content
                was RE-READ since each source changed, not that the re-reading
                concluded anything. --update without re-reading defeats it (R4).

    covenant    @gate_covenant_hash
      checks    sha recomputed from the canonical covenant vs each witness,
                BY CLASS — mutable ▪ derived ▪ tool-managed ▪ provenance
      blocking  YES ▪ registry: @covenant_registry
      not covers   provenance stamps — reported, never judged. ∄ reliable local
                signal for 'a promotion happened'; what guarantees stamps are
                not rewritten is sync_covenant_hash.sh refusing the class.
      note      reads NO shared config, deliberately — a verifier reading the
                same source as the thing it verifies compares a value to
                itself (covenant_hash_registry §design_note).

    symbols     @gate_symbols
      checks    D7 (∀ doc ∈ system/ is English, covenant.vsm exempt) ▪ glyphs
                used but declared nowhere ▪ duplicate identifier definitions ▪
                R_ref_resolution both ways: ∄ dangling @var, ∄ orphan bind ▪
                density (prose % ▪ words/line)
      blocking  YES for --undeclared ▪ ADVISORY for --density
      not covers   whether an identifier MEANS what its namespace says — it sees
                that a namespaced identifier is declared once; it cannot see
                that the formula under it contradicts its own comment.
                // was `A8.vOS` — a live EXAMPLE, declared in theory/ and not in
                // boot/. An illustration must not create a dependency the boot
                // set cannot resolve on its own.
      note      the D7 axis reads prose WORDS. annotation tokens (channel and
                experimenter roles, since renamed) sat inside a CERTIFIED
                document and were caught by the directive allowlist, not by
                --d7: an annotation token is neither prose nor a word that
                axis scores.

    code_lang   @gate_code_language
      checks    foreign script ANYWHERE in a code file — the NATURAL_SCRIPT
                axis (CJK, Cyrillic, kana, ...), emoji and declared notation
                NOT foreign — plus Spanish in comments/docstrings by the
                house marker rule (2+ SPANISH, or SPANISH_STRONG, or an
                accented word outside ACCENT_OK), quoted spans exempt per
                comment block so a literal rmw3 citation survives
                translation
      blocking  YES ▪ corpus: .py .ts .js .rs .sh .go (EXCLUDE_DIRS out)
      not covers   string literals and user-facing TUI text — Spanish UI
                stays allowed (S5 directive 2026-09-27), only comments,
                docstrings and identifiers are in scope. Whether an
                identifier is English is not judged: a foreign word scores
                clean unless it is in the marker list —
                OTHER_LATIN_LANG_UNCHECKED, declared (this axis sees
                Spanish, not French).
      waives    a line carrying `foreign-script-allow:` or
                `spanish-allow:` — detector-guts convention, the mirror of
                hardcoded-allow: a detector that cannot show its own
                example is a detector nobody can read.

    docs_lang   @gate_docs_language
      checks    foreign script in every .vsm/.md (same NATURAL_SCRIPT
                axis) ▪ D7 English over system/**/*.vsm by the house rule,
                covenant.vsm exempt
      blocking  YES ▪ corpus: docs (script axis, all layers) ▪ system/ (D7)
      not covers   docs OUTSIDE system/ — transient and local layers are
                language-persistent in Spanish (S5 directive 2026-09-27).
                Also not whether the English is CORRECT — only that it is
                neither Spanish nor generation garbage.
      note      reads system/ directly (the ~119-document tree), so it does
                not inherit the stale --d7 CORPUS (1 file) — D7-CORPUS-STALE,
                open. Harness-run, not only on-write: the hook catches the
                editor, this gate catches the archive.

    grammar     @vsl_parser — the reference parser for C2
      checks    header ▪ @vsm ▪ block shape ▪ (--strict) footer, brace depth,
                @ref targets, @status proposed, domain_context layer
      blocking  NO — REPORT ONLY, and measured: without --strict the parser
                accepts literal garbage; with --strict, 13 of 40 CERTIFIED
                documents were INVALID and EVERY class was a known exception
                or a false positive.
      not covers   the grammar it is named for. Its BNF was STALE against the
                corpus in three places — LIFESTATUS: RESOLVED 2026-08-09: all three were
                the GRAMMAR being narrower than its own canon, not the documents
                being wrong.
      // VSL-PARSER-BNF-STALE — CLOSED 2026-08-09: --strict went from 13 of
      // 40 INVALID to 1 of 48, and the gate now BLOCKS on staged files. The
      // one left is a real broken ref in covenant — COVENANT-REF-BROKEN.",
}
⟦ /validation_gates ⟧